}]}]}]}}],"rule":"weight + residual_pack - 0.25*max(0,residual_cover-residual_pack) - 0.35*(0.5*neighbor_pack+0.5*neighbor_cover)/(1+max(0,boundary_weight)/max(1e-9,abs(conflict_weight))/(1+2*max(0,residual_edge_weight)/max(1e-9,abs(compatible_weight)))) - 0.01*weight*degree/max(1,1+degree)","rationale":"The identical parents share an inclusion-lookahead backbone: root reward, residual packing and cover estimates, neighborhood opportunity cost, and edge-structure corrections. This variant treats the residual cover-minus-pack gap as uncertainty to penalize rather than optimistic reward. It estimates blocked neighborhood value using a packing/cover midpoint, then discounts that cost when neighbors strongly conflict with retained vertices, adjusting for residual conflict density. The thought is to favor credible completions while recognizing that blocked alternatives may already compete with the residual schedule."}